    "body": "## Purpose\n\nWith `--return-sampling-mask`, a request with `temperature <= 0` or `top_k <= 0` fails with HTTP 500 and an empty message (`{\"message\": \"\", \"type\": \"InternalServerError\"}`). The cause is that `InputProcessor._validate_params` raises a plain `ValueError` for these two checks. `AsyncLLM.generate` only re-raises `VLLMClientError`, so it wraps the `ValueError` in an empty `EngineGenerateError`. Clients see a 500 and get no reason. For example, chat requests that use the default `top_k=0` all fail this way.\n\nFix: raise `VLLMValidationError` (with `parameter`/`value`), the same as the other request checks in `_validate_params`. The client then gets a 400 that states the reason.\n\nRelated: #61322 changes the message text of the same checks but keeps `ValueError`, so those requests would still return 500.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n`pytest tests/v1/engine/test_input_processor_trace_replay.py`: the new parametrized test fails on main and passes with this change.\n\nReproduced on v0.31.0 with Qwen3-30B-A3B and `--return-sampling-mask`. A `/v1/chat/completions` or `/inference/v1/generate` request without `top_k` returned 500 with an empty message. With `top_k` set, the same requests returned 200.\n\nAI assistance (Claude) was used; all changes were reviewed by the submitter.\n",
